1
00:00:02,169 --> 00:00:03,409
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,604 --> 00:00:05,800
<i>I'm assuming the
captaincy of Gotham Central.</i>

3
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:09,841
HARVEY: You just better hope
you can pay up when your bill's due.

4
00:00:10,110 --> 00:00:11,544
And it'll come due.

5
00:00:14,581 --> 00:00:16,345
ALFRED: <i>Let me know
how I can help you.</i>

6
00:00:17,417 --> 00:00:18,908
BRUCE: <i>Stop trying
to be my father.</i>

7
00:00:20,821 --> 00:00:22,084
(GROANS)

8
00:00:24,057 --> 00:00:25,457
ALFRED: <i>Master
Bruce, I'm so sorry.</i>

9
00:00:26,226 --> 00:00:27,421
Alfred, you're fired.

10
00:00:30,464 --> 00:00:31,557
This is your turf now.

11
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,467
NYGMA: <i>You're new
leader of The Narrows.</i>

12
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,369
I am in control!

13
00:00:38,639 --> 00:00:40,005
(LAUGHS WICKEDLY)

14
00:00:40,073 --> 00:00:41,433
You're in love with
Lee Thompkins,

15
00:00:41,475 --> 00:00:42,499
you pathetic loser.

16
00:00:42,576 --> 00:00:43,737
Shut up!

17
00:00:47,214 --> 00:00:48,443
Where are they?

18
00:00:48,582 --> 00:00:50,050
MAN: <i>That's powerful stuff.</i>

19
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:51,918
<i>It can get in your DNA.</i>

20
00:00:54,021 --> 00:00:55,532
TABITHA: <i>You're gonna
remember me, Butch...</i>

21
00:00:55,556 --> 00:00:56,956
(CLANGS)

22
00:00:57,057 --> 00:00:58,057
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

23
00:00:58,125 --> 00:00:59,218
<i>I tried.</i>

24
00:01:00,994 --> 00:01:02,434
BUTCH: <i>What the
hell happened to me?</i>

25
00:01:06,767 --> 00:01:07,826
(GUNSHOT)

26
00:01:09,002 --> 00:01:10,061
GORDON: <i>That was you.</i>

27
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:11,900
<i>You sent this
monster to my city?</i>

28
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:14,019
HARVEY: <i>I heard you got the Pyg.</i>

29
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:15,368
Turned out well.

30
00:01:15,442 --> 00:01:16,705
You didn't even need me...

31
00:01:19,146 --> 00:01:21,980
They, uh, believe in
you. Don't let them down.

32
00:01:32,259 --> 00:01:34,353
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

33
00:01:37,531 --> 00:01:39,466
(MUSIC PLAYING ON RECORD)

34
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:45,800
WOMAN: How can I
help you, Captain Gordon?

35
00:01:46,139 --> 00:01:48,335
I assure you this is a
respectable establishment.

36
00:01:48,442 --> 00:01:50,434
Relax, I'm not here
to shut you down.

37
00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:51,603
I'm looking for someone.

38
00:01:51,678 --> 00:01:53,670
We are trusted
for our discretion.

39
00:01:53,847 --> 00:01:54,974
Mmm-hmm.

40
00:01:57,684 --> 00:01:58,777
Was he here?

41
00:01:58,852 --> 00:02:00,343
Who did he spend the night with?

42
00:02:00,454 --> 00:02:02,787
He specifically requested
Tallulah and Pip.

43
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:07,322
That's him.

44
00:02:07,561 --> 00:02:08,654
That's Bullock.

45
00:02:09,162 --> 00:02:10,391
If he comes back,

46
00:02:10,597 --> 00:02:13,499
please tell him to call me.

47
00:02:17,938 --> 00:02:19,634
(TRAIN PASSING)

48
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:38,315
(UNLOCKING DOOR)

49
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:44,297
It was an old
Chinese guy's place,

50
00:02:44,364 --> 00:02:45,684
filled with rare
drugs and stuff.

51
00:02:45,766 --> 00:02:47,928
He split town.
Place is empty now.

52
00:02:49,169 --> 00:02:51,070
Where are the drugs?
You said there'd be drugs.

53
00:02:54,574 --> 00:02:55,735
Holy crap.

54
00:02:59,179 --> 00:03:00,374
What the...

55
00:03:02,549 --> 00:03:03,915
Don't touch it, dude.

56
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:07,612
(SQUELCHING)

57
00:03:10,023 --> 00:03:11,321
MAN: You just woke it up.

58
00:03:41,822 --> 00:03:45,224
Hey, Tiffany, who's
the stiff at the counter?

59
00:03:45,392 --> 00:03:47,759
New customer, nice guy, polite.

60
00:03:48,361 --> 00:03:49,590
Leave him alone, okay?

61
00:03:51,698 --> 00:03:53,792
Hey, new guy?

62
00:03:55,202 --> 00:03:56,363
Do I know you?

63
00:03:56,703 --> 00:03:59,104
No, mate. Most definitely not.

64
00:04:00,273 --> 00:04:01,571
Not from around here, huh?

65
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:05,602
And what gave you that idea?

66
00:04:12,552 --> 00:04:15,215
Here, miss. Thank you very much.

67
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:17,083
Keep the change.

68
00:04:18,458 --> 00:04:21,121
That stiff's shoes are
worth more than my car.

69
00:04:27,167 --> 00:04:28,635
(DOOR OPENS)

70
00:04:39,613 --> 00:04:41,548
LEE: <i>I understand
times are tough.</i>

71
00:04:41,982 --> 00:04:44,451
I understand you
need to make a living.

72
00:04:45,385 --> 00:04:48,082
But it's time to stop
punishing each other

73
00:04:48,155 --> 00:04:51,319
for the situation the
city has put you in.

74
00:04:51,892 --> 00:04:55,522
Instead of stealing from
those hurting as much as you,

75
00:04:56,496 --> 00:05:00,194
this community needs to
start protecting one another.

76
00:05:00,534 --> 00:05:02,628
We do what we do to survive!

77
00:05:02,702 --> 00:05:03,795
ALL: Yeah.

78
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,500
And is that all you
want, all of you?

79
00:05:07,107 --> 00:05:09,941
Just to survive every
day, one day at a time?

80
00:05:10,343 --> 00:05:13,575
Listen, Doc, down here,
it's every man for himself!

81
00:05:13,747 --> 00:05:14,924
That's the way it's always been!

82
00:05:14,948 --> 00:05:16,849
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

83
00:05:22,455 --> 00:05:23,753
How many of you have kids?

84
00:05:26,126 --> 00:05:27,651
I've been running
a clinic down here

85
00:05:27,727 --> 00:05:28,854
for the last nine months,

86
00:05:29,196 --> 00:05:31,859
and I have been treating
your kids for things like TB,

87
00:05:32,365 --> 00:05:34,800
hepatitis, pertussis, pneumonia.

88
00:05:35,202 --> 00:05:38,798
Diseases that don't
belong in a modern city.

89
00:05:39,306 --> 00:05:41,639
But there are no functioning
hospitals down here,

90
00:05:41,808 --> 00:05:44,300
and doctors are
too afraid to visit.

91
00:05:45,278 --> 00:05:47,213
You're not stealing
from the rich,

92
00:05:47,314 --> 00:05:49,114
- you're stealing from each other.
- (TICKING)

93
00:05:49,683 --> 00:05:51,481
You are fighting each other,

94
00:05:52,819 --> 00:05:55,812
and you are living in a prison
of your own construction.

95
00:05:57,057 --> 00:05:59,253
MAN: Well, hello,
beautiful. What's your name?

96
00:06:03,864 --> 00:06:04,991
Ivy.

97
00:06:06,833 --> 00:06:08,233
My name was Ivy.

98
00:06:09,269 --> 00:06:10,498
Well, Ivy,

99
00:06:12,072 --> 00:06:14,837
what's a nice girl like you
doing in a place like this?

100
00:06:14,908 --> 00:06:15,908
(SCREAMS)

101
00:06:16,009 --> 00:06:17,375
(MUFFLED GROANS)

102
00:06:18,979 --> 00:06:21,210
(SHUSHING)

103
00:06:25,352 --> 00:06:28,345
Well, that's a hell of a thing.

104
00:06:31,758 --> 00:06:32,953
Let's go!

105
00:06:34,961 --> 00:06:36,088
(DOOR CLOSES)

106
00:06:55,382 --> 00:06:56,850
Extraordinary.

107
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:01,713
MAN: Hey.

108
00:07:02,322 --> 00:07:03,654
Little Lord Fuddy-duddy.

109
00:07:05,158 --> 00:07:06,456
It's Fauntleroy.

110
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:08,054
What?

111
00:07:08,128 --> 00:07:11,121
<i>Little Lord Fauntleroy</i> by
Frances Hodgson Burnett.

112
00:07:12,065 --> 00:07:13,658
A tad saccharin for my tastes...

113
00:07:13,767 --> 00:07:16,635
Shut up. Wallet, watch, jewelry.

114
00:07:17,137 --> 00:07:18,137
Absolutely not.

115
00:07:18,238 --> 00:07:20,198
I mean, you're a big man,
but you're out of shape.

116
00:07:20,740 --> 00:07:22,606
And what, you're
three beers in already?

117
00:07:26,079 --> 00:07:27,240
GORDON: That's enough!

118
00:07:28,715 --> 00:07:29,739
Get out of here.

119
00:07:36,256 --> 00:07:38,418
Not who I was
expecting to see here.

120
00:07:39,659 --> 00:07:40,752
Likewise.

121
00:07:41,261 --> 00:07:42,301
GORDON: Is Bruce with you?

122
00:07:43,663 --> 00:07:44,687
No.

123
00:07:45,498 --> 00:07:46,727
What are you doing here?

124
00:07:46,933 --> 00:07:49,903
Well, it's not too
bad down here really.

125
00:07:50,236 --> 00:07:51,414
I mean, you can
rent a lovely space

126
00:07:51,438 --> 00:07:52,599
for next to nothing,

127
00:07:52,672 --> 00:07:54,436
if you move around
and you're patient.

128
00:07:55,075 --> 00:07:56,168
You live here?

129
00:07:57,477 --> 00:07:58,501
Nearby.

130
00:08:01,114 --> 00:08:02,343
It's a long story.

131
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:08,315
Give me the chance
to prove to you

132
00:08:08,455 --> 00:08:09,479
(MAN COUGHS)

133
00:08:09,556 --> 00:08:11,650
that I can turn The
Narrows into a place

134
00:08:11,725 --> 00:08:14,456
where you don't have to
steal from one another to live.

135
00:08:16,997 --> 00:08:18,124
Yes.

136
00:08:19,366 --> 00:08:20,425
CROWD: Yeah.

137
00:08:20,867 --> 00:08:21,926
Yeah.

138
00:08:22,135 --> 00:08:24,627
(CROWD CLAPPING AND CHEERING)

139
00:08:28,775 --> 00:08:30,209
(TICKING)

140
00:08:36,049 --> 00:08:37,347
(ENGINE REVVING)

141
00:08:40,653 --> 00:08:41,677
(GRUNTS)

142
00:08:44,858 --> 00:08:46,656
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

143
00:08:52,232 --> 00:08:53,894
(ALL COUGHING)

144
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,093
All right.

145
00:08:55,502 --> 00:08:56,697
Go, come on.

146
00:08:56,770 --> 00:08:58,170
Go, go, go.

147
00:08:58,338 --> 00:08:59,601
Go. Go.

148
00:09:01,908 --> 00:09:04,241
Everyone, move
away from the building!

149
00:09:05,045 --> 00:09:07,014
(ALARM BLARING)

150
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,742
- (SIREN WAILING)
- (INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)

151
00:09:26,766 --> 00:09:28,394
GORDON: There's
your mom. Go ahead.

152
00:09:28,501 --> 00:09:29,560
Mommy!

153
00:09:29,669 --> 00:09:30,728
That's the last one.

154
00:09:30,837 --> 00:09:31,877
- Building's clear.
- Okay.

155
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:33,567
- (MAN COUGHING)
- Oxygen. Please.

156
00:09:33,673 --> 00:09:34,873
OFFICER: Over here, over here.

157
00:09:35,108 --> 00:09:37,077
Listen up. We need
to set up a perimeter,

158
00:09:37,143 --> 00:09:39,237
and start interviewing
witnesses. Let's go.

159
00:09:40,447 --> 00:09:41,647
ALFRED: Well, they seem on it.

160
00:09:42,382 --> 00:09:45,375
Appears like you turned around
the GCPD, Captain Gordon.

161
00:09:45,652 --> 00:09:46,745
LUCIUS: Gordon!

162
00:09:47,287 --> 00:09:49,119
Quite a mess. Thought
you might need help.

163
00:09:49,322 --> 00:09:51,791
Thank you. We need to
find the source of the blast.

164
00:09:52,325 --> 00:09:53,602
Alfred, I do want
to talk to you,

165
00:09:53,626 --> 00:09:55,026
but I have to
deal with this first.

166
00:09:55,095 --> 00:09:57,155
- You have my number. Call me.
- All right.

167
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:58,322
Let's go.

168
00:10:01,835 --> 00:10:04,600
GORDON: I'll ask you one
more time. Why were you here?

169
00:10:05,939 --> 00:10:07,737
It was a wine and cheese
mixer. (CHUCKLES)

170
00:10:08,541 --> 00:10:10,601
Laugh all you want.
They were trying to kill you.

171
00:10:10,810 --> 00:10:14,372
This is The Narrows, bud.
That's every day around here.

172
00:10:15,115 --> 00:10:17,914
MAN: Yeah, just another
beautiful day in The Narrows, Cap.

173
00:10:18,818 --> 00:10:19,945
LUCIUS: Gordon.

174
00:10:21,154 --> 00:10:22,247
Get him out of here.

175
00:10:23,056 --> 00:10:24,217
What you got?

176
00:10:24,390 --> 00:10:26,586
Well, it seems like a
piece of a toy plane.

177
00:10:26,659 --> 00:10:28,287
And, yet, if I'm not mistaken,

178
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:31,162
it's covered in plastic
explosive residue.

179
00:10:31,498 --> 00:10:34,627
There's also the remnants of
what seems like a trigger wire.

180
00:10:35,802 --> 00:10:36,929
Whoever built it,

181
00:10:37,003 --> 00:10:39,199
takes pride in their work
and has considerable talent,

182
00:10:39,339 --> 00:10:41,433
historical knowledge
even. Look at the detail.

183
00:10:45,044 --> 00:10:46,205
Pretty elaborate.

184
00:10:47,213 --> 00:10:48,442
I can think of easier ways

185
00:10:48,515 --> 00:10:50,780
to kill a room full of
criminals than with a toy plane.

186
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:53,317
Perhaps, it was intended
to fly to someone specific

187
00:10:53,386 --> 00:10:54,877
and not destroy the whole room.

188
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:56,880
Like an assassination attempt?

189
00:10:58,124 --> 00:10:59,956
If so, who was the target?

190
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:07,023
Whoever this was, needs
to be made an example of.

191
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:09,963
I mean, can't they tell
you were trying to help.

192
00:11:10,036 --> 00:11:12,596
- Maybe it wasn't one of them.
- Oh, of course, it was.

193
00:11:12,872 --> 00:11:14,950
I just think that maybe the
best thing for The Narrows

194
00:11:14,974 --> 00:11:17,307
is to burn it to the
ground! Start over.

195
00:11:17,377 --> 00:11:19,455
Well, that would certainly
suit everyone, wouldn't it?

196
00:11:19,479 --> 00:11:22,278
I'm just saying someone
tried to blow you to bits,

197
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:23,828
and I bet they're
gonna try it again!

198
00:11:23,883 --> 00:11:26,512
So I'm going to find
them, and when I do,

199
00:11:26,653 --> 00:11:29,384
Grundy's going to pull
them apart, limb by limb!

200
00:11:29,489 --> 00:11:30,616
Isn't that right, big fella?

201
00:11:31,791 --> 00:11:33,191
Hey, Grundy?

202
00:11:36,396 --> 00:11:37,455
You okay?

203
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:42,558
Okay.

204
00:11:44,671 --> 00:11:45,730
(NYGMA SIGHS)

205
00:11:46,573 --> 00:11:47,666
(DOOR OPENS)

206
00:11:50,276 --> 00:11:51,835
- (SLASHES)
- (SCREAMS)

207
00:11:53,246 --> 00:11:54,544
My name is Butch.

208
00:11:55,748 --> 00:11:56,772
(GUNSHOT)

209
00:11:59,686 --> 00:12:00,915
Butch Gilzean.

210
00:12:03,923 --> 00:12:05,084
MAN: There he is.

211
00:12:05,191 --> 00:12:06,284
(APPLAUDING)

212
00:12:10,730 --> 00:12:12,221
That was so brave, sir.

213
00:12:12,699 --> 00:12:14,167
It's Alfred, please.

214
00:12:16,369 --> 00:12:17,428
It's the good stuff.

215
00:12:17,604 --> 00:12:19,436
Our manager hides
it in his drawer.

216
00:12:19,539 --> 00:12:20,563
ALFRED: Thank you.

217
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:22,064
On the house.

218
00:12:25,378 --> 00:12:26,573
(SIGHS)

219
00:12:29,616 --> 00:12:30,743
What you did out there,

220
00:12:33,519 --> 00:12:35,181
running into a
burning building...

221
00:12:35,688 --> 00:12:37,122
Well, I wouldn't have done it.

222
00:12:38,558 --> 00:12:39,924
No hard feelings, eh?

223
00:12:40,927 --> 00:12:42,020
No.

224
00:12:42,395 --> 00:12:43,454
Good man.

225
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:45,621
Thanks.

226
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:48,132
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

227
00:12:49,302 --> 00:12:50,326
Cheers.

228
00:12:55,241 --> 00:12:56,436
ALFRED: What happened there?

229
00:12:56,809 --> 00:12:58,607
I fell. No big deal.

230
00:13:13,593 --> 00:13:14,953
There are a few
places in the city

231
00:13:14,994 --> 00:13:16,553
that collect and
sell antique toys,

232
00:13:16,663 --> 00:13:19,258
but only this one also
manufactures its own.

233
00:13:22,568 --> 00:13:23,934
(BELLS CHIMING)

234
00:13:24,304 --> 00:13:26,296
(TOYS WHIRRING)

235
00:13:29,108 --> 00:13:31,668
(TOY CACKLING)

236
00:13:32,412 --> 00:13:33,412
Um...

237
00:13:33,479 --> 00:13:35,311
Can I help you, gentlemen?

238
00:13:35,448 --> 00:13:36,507
LUCIUS: Yes.

239
00:13:37,150 --> 00:13:39,585
We were wondering if
you recognized this plane?

240
00:13:39,852 --> 00:13:40,979
One of yours?

241
00:13:44,957 --> 00:13:46,118
Where did you find it?

242
00:13:46,192 --> 00:13:47,319
Yours or not?

243
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:50,953
It's a pine and lead
1944 Mustang replica.

244
00:13:51,864 --> 00:13:56,325
We have these, yes,
but it's been altered.

245
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:58,399
To carry a bomb, yeah.

246
00:13:59,238 --> 00:14:00,598
GORDON: How many
people work here?

247
00:14:01,574 --> 00:14:03,304
Just me and my father.

248
00:14:03,376 --> 00:14:04,639
GORDON: And where is he?

249
00:14:04,977 --> 00:14:06,036
Upstairs.

250
00:14:06,546 --> 00:14:07,707
Go get him.

251
00:14:13,886 --> 00:14:15,548
LUCIUS: Got a hunch
you'd like to share?

252
00:14:15,722 --> 00:14:16,883
No.

253
00:14:17,156 --> 00:14:18,351
Just a bad feeling.

254
00:14:22,061 --> 00:14:23,654
Of course, I'd happily be wrong.

255
00:14:23,963 --> 00:14:26,330
(SIGHS) Who buys these things?

256
00:14:27,133 --> 00:14:28,610
GORDON: I'm not
sure any of it is for sale.

257
00:14:28,634 --> 00:14:30,227
I don't see price
tags on anything.

258
00:14:31,571 --> 00:14:32,731
LUCIUS: Any word from Harvey?

259
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:34,740
Not yet.

260
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:38,345
Think he'll return to the GCPD?

261
00:14:39,746 --> 00:14:42,147
To be honest, I'm not sure.

262
00:14:42,348 --> 00:14:43,543
LUCIUS: Um...

263
00:14:43,683 --> 00:14:45,083
- Gordon...
- Get down!

264
00:14:46,219 --> 00:14:47,619
(GUNSHOTS)

265
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:58,262
ROBOT: Seek and destroy.

266
00:14:58,364 --> 00:14:59,855
Seek and destroy.

267
00:14:59,932 --> 00:15:01,400
Seek and destroy.

268
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:02,796
Seek and destroy.

269
00:15:06,305 --> 00:15:07,739
Seek and destroy.

270
00:15:07,807 --> 00:15:09,241
- Seek and destroy.
- (BEEPING)

271
00:15:09,542 --> 00:15:11,374
You've got to be kidding me.

272
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:13,940
(BOMB BEEPS)

273
00:15:24,257 --> 00:15:26,522
Wait, wait. No, no, wait,
wait, wait. Come on, he's...

274
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:27,924
He's my father.

275
00:15:31,731 --> 00:15:32,960
I can't let you hurt him.

276
00:15:37,637 --> 00:15:40,732
I swear to God, I had no
idea what my father was up to.

277
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,465
There's a machine gun built into

278
00:15:42,575 --> 00:15:44,476
the wooden hand of
this nutcracker here.

279
00:15:44,811 --> 00:15:46,355
Excuse me if I find
that hard to believe.

280
00:15:46,379 --> 00:15:48,041
I didn't know, okay?

281
00:15:48,414 --> 00:15:50,781
My father, he hates
to be disturbed.

282
00:15:51,117 --> 00:15:53,985
He also built a bomb that almost
blew up a building this morning.

283
00:15:54,086 --> 00:15:55,179
We need to know why.

284
00:15:55,288 --> 00:15:57,086
- Who was the target?
- I don't know.

285
00:15:57,156 --> 00:15:59,076
LUCIUS: Has anyone
suspicious been here recently,

286
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:00,753
asking for specialty toys?

287
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:03,659
No one comes in here,
this is just his workshop.

288
00:16:03,830 --> 00:16:05,025
He mostly works at night.

289
00:16:05,131 --> 00:16:08,295
See, he boxes the
things he makes and

290
00:16:09,101 --> 00:16:10,262
ships them.

291
00:16:10,436 --> 00:16:11,460
What?

292
00:16:12,305 --> 00:16:13,500
Like, three days ago,

293
00:16:13,606 --> 00:16:16,337
I thought I heard him talking
to someone behind his door.

294
00:16:16,476 --> 00:16:20,140
His voice was low, like he
didn't want me to hear him.

295
00:16:20,313 --> 00:16:21,611
Did you hear a name?

296
00:16:21,681 --> 00:16:23,775
I heard my father
repeat something,

297
00:16:23,850 --> 00:16:25,819
like he was confirming a name.

298
00:16:25,918 --> 00:16:27,978
He said, "The Doc."

299
00:16:28,688 --> 00:16:30,418
The Doc? Who's that?

300
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:32,485
I have no idea.

301
00:16:33,192 --> 00:16:34,455
(SIREN WAILING)

302
00:16:34,527 --> 00:16:35,756
Hey, can you deal with this?

303
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:38,127
I'm gonna talk to somebody
who might know who the Doc is.

304
00:16:41,834 --> 00:16:42,858
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

305
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:19,668
This place is killing you.

306
00:17:19,739 --> 00:17:21,416
- (HONKING)
- WOMAN: Honey, the taxi is here.

307
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:22,635
MAN: Let's go.

308
00:17:23,476 --> 00:17:24,910
WOMAN: If we are late...

309
00:17:25,144 --> 00:17:27,238
MAN: We need to
pack the other stuff...

310
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:29,358
WOMAN: Okay. Of
course it's my fault.

311
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:31,874
MAN: You only need,
like, five pairs of shoes.

312
00:17:31,984 --> 00:17:33,043
WOMAN: Come on.

313
00:17:33,219 --> 00:17:34,380
Let's go. Let's go.

314
00:17:35,588 --> 00:17:37,028
- (CAR DOOR CLOSES)
- (ENGINE STARTS)

315
00:18:27,206 --> 00:18:28,469
(TV REMOTE CLICKS)

316
00:18:28,574 --> 00:18:30,852
REPORTER ON TV: <i>the truck
overturned spilling its load of gasoline</i>

317
00:18:30,876 --> 00:18:32,242
<i>into Gotham's Nature Park.</i>

318
00:18:32,411 --> 00:18:35,609
<i>The GCPD is warning all
citizens to remain clear of the...</i>

319
00:18:35,715 --> 00:18:37,875
MAN ON TV: <i>causing gas
to leak into the water supply</i>

320
00:18:37,917 --> 00:18:38,917
<i>which then ignited,</i>

321
00:18:38,985 --> 00:18:40,817
<i>setting fire to the
resident's kitchen</i>

322
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:42,786
<i>which set off a 24-acre blaze.</i>

323
00:18:42,888 --> 00:18:44,584
<i>Wayne Enterprises can't...</i>

324
00:18:45,625 --> 00:18:48,789
WOMAN ON TV: <i>Now, there's no
reason to ever be alone in this city again.</i>

325
00:18:49,328 --> 00:18:52,662
<i>The Sirens Club is
back, with a passion.</i>

326
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:57,793
<i>Ladies drink for
free whilst men don't.</i>

327
00:18:59,271 --> 00:19:01,467
<i>You'll like it. It's nice.</i>

328
00:19:02,174 --> 00:19:03,665
I know you.

329
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,006
All of you.

330
00:19:10,716 --> 00:19:12,947
And I'm pretty sure I hated you.

331
00:19:16,522 --> 00:19:18,013
(WOMAN LAUGHS)

332
00:19:18,357 --> 00:19:19,825
You're funny, Alfred.

333
00:19:20,826 --> 00:19:22,317
I honestly haven't
laughed this much

334
00:19:22,395 --> 00:19:23,829
in a very long time.

335
00:19:23,896 --> 00:19:25,990
I'm glad I'm able to
amuse you, Ms. Gale.

336
00:19:26,499 --> 00:19:28,661
- Your accent, I love it.
- (DOG BARKING)

337
00:19:29,135 --> 00:19:30,262
Where are you from?

338
00:19:30,436 --> 00:19:33,634
A charming place called
Whitechapel in East End, London.

339
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:35,501
Go back often?

340
00:19:36,475 --> 00:19:37,670
No.

341
00:19:37,777 --> 00:19:39,006
Sadly, no.

342
00:19:39,478 --> 00:19:41,344
Well, perhaps, you should.

343
00:19:42,515 --> 00:19:43,608
Why did you leave?

344
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,284
Well, I was in the military.

345
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:48,430
I was really proud
to serve my country,

346
00:19:48,454 --> 00:19:49,665
not so proud of
some of the things

347
00:19:49,689 --> 00:19:50,689
we had to do, though.

348
00:19:51,457 --> 00:19:55,292
And when I left, I
found myself, um, lost.

349
00:19:55,895 --> 00:19:58,057
You know, it was
a tough transition.

350
00:19:59,331 --> 00:20:02,699
Then I met this man
who changed my life.

351
00:20:03,536 --> 00:20:05,368
He brought me to
America, gave me a job.

352
00:20:05,838 --> 00:20:07,534
And where is that man now?

353
00:20:08,541 --> 00:20:09,565
He's dead.

354
00:20:11,711 --> 00:20:13,009
And I miss him.

355
00:20:14,413 --> 00:20:15,881
I miss him very much.

356
00:20:16,248 --> 00:20:17,443
(VEHICLE ARRIVING)

357
00:20:18,384 --> 00:20:19,784
(BRAKES SCREECHING)

358
00:20:21,454 --> 00:20:22,717
Who's that, your boyfriend?

359
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:26,086
MAN: Hey, you
didn't call me back.

360
00:20:26,192 --> 00:20:27,832
I was heading to the
diner to pick you up.

361
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:29,088
Oh, that wasn't necessary.

362
00:20:29,195 --> 00:20:31,164
Alfred was kind enough
to walk me home.

363
00:20:32,932 --> 00:20:34,025
Thank you, sir.

364
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:36,865
I hate to think of Tiff alone
on these streets after dark.

365
00:20:39,705 --> 00:20:40,832
(WOMAN SCREAMS)

366
00:20:41,373 --> 00:20:43,899
Drop the act, sunshine.
I've seen her face!

367
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:45,935
It was your idea, was it?

368
00:20:46,212 --> 00:20:48,340
Wear her hair down
and cover the bruising?

369
00:20:48,414 --> 00:20:51,384
Oh, my. What a little
tattletale she's been.

370
00:20:51,450 --> 00:20:53,851
- What am I to do with her?
- TIFFANY: Stop it!

371
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:55,263
Don't make things
worse. I can handle it.

372
00:20:55,287 --> 00:20:57,518
Listen to me!
Listen! Listen to me!

373
00:20:57,690 --> 00:20:58,690
You stay away from him.

374
00:20:58,758 --> 00:21:00,238
He's dangerous. Let
me walk you home.

375
00:21:00,392 --> 00:21:01,553
I'll be fine.

376
00:21:09,602 --> 00:21:13,596
MAN: Oh, Tiffany, what did I tell
you about talking to strange men?

377
00:21:13,773 --> 00:21:17,073
It's time to go. We
have so much to discuss.

378
00:21:26,519 --> 00:21:27,612
You be careful.

379
00:21:30,990 --> 00:21:32,322
(ENGINE REVVING)

380
00:21:33,425 --> 00:21:34,484
(DOG YELPS)

381
00:21:39,732 --> 00:21:41,462
There was a fatality
at the bomb site.

382
00:21:41,567 --> 00:21:44,230
A young man found in a room
below the impact site and...

383
00:21:44,503 --> 00:21:46,836
- Well, perhaps I should just show you.
- Of course.

384
00:21:46,939 --> 00:21:47,939
Yeah. (CLEARS THROAT)

385
00:21:49,241 --> 00:21:51,904
The cause of death
was ingested poison.

386
00:21:51,977 --> 00:21:54,469
Now, see the discoloration
around the mouth?

387
00:21:55,014 --> 00:21:57,609
LUCIUS: The poison entered
directly into the bloodstream?

388
00:21:57,917 --> 00:21:59,681
But see, that's
not what's unusual.

389
00:22:00,352 --> 00:22:01,581
There seems to be something

390
00:22:01,654 --> 00:22:03,714
emanating from
within the victim's body.

391
00:22:03,823 --> 00:22:05,951
Time of death was
several hours ago,

392
00:22:06,025 --> 00:22:08,722
but this foreign,
organic material

393
00:22:08,828 --> 00:22:11,525
is not only alive but growing.

394
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:13,393
LUCIUS: Seems like moss.

395
00:22:13,499 --> 00:22:15,195
CORONER: Toxicodendron radicans.

396
00:22:15,301 --> 00:22:16,633
Poison ivy?

397
00:22:16,702 --> 00:22:20,730
Yes, and microscopic at
first but multiplying, growing.

398
00:22:21,340 --> 00:22:23,900
Living off the
victim's dead tissue.

399
00:22:35,221 --> 00:22:36,553
Fascinating.

400
00:22:39,725 --> 00:22:41,193
(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)

401
00:22:42,828 --> 00:22:44,387
(PEOPLE LAUGHING)

402
00:22:58,844 --> 00:23:00,369
BARBARA: So the
commercial worked.

403
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:02,314
We're back and busier than ever.

404
00:23:02,381 --> 00:23:03,815
Good, 'cause
that's the last time

405
00:23:03,883 --> 00:23:05,044
you're getting me on camera.

406
00:23:05,150 --> 00:23:06,174
Who's that?

407
00:23:07,353 --> 00:23:08,377
BARBARA: Who's who?

408
00:23:09,922 --> 00:23:11,447
- (GLASS SHATTERING)
- (BARBARA SIGHS)

409
00:23:11,924 --> 00:23:14,450
Selina, will you tell
those brats over there

410
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:15,560
to keep it down?

411
00:23:17,596 --> 00:23:18,620
SELINA: Why me?

412
00:23:18,931 --> 00:23:20,957
Because you're a partner now,

413
00:23:21,066 --> 00:23:24,036
and also, the one
paying is a friend of yours.

414
00:23:35,414 --> 00:23:36,473
Bruce.

415
00:23:38,117 --> 00:23:39,176
What's up?

416
00:23:39,285 --> 00:23:40,446
Champagne?

417
00:23:40,686 --> 00:23:42,348
- No.
- Why?

418
00:23:42,855 --> 00:23:45,017
They don't card you
here, and even if they did,

419
00:23:45,958 --> 00:23:47,187
this is Gotham.

420
00:23:48,093 --> 00:23:49,356
By "they" you mean me.

421
00:23:50,129 --> 00:23:51,563
This is my place, too.

422
00:23:52,031 --> 00:23:53,966
- Really?
- Yeah.

423
00:23:54,066 --> 00:23:55,744
So you wanna tell
your little brat pack here

424
00:23:55,768 --> 00:23:58,397
to reel it in a little, or
should I call your keeper?

425
00:23:58,704 --> 00:24:01,139
Go ahead, call Alfred,
he won't answer.

426
00:24:01,874 --> 00:24:02,898
Why?

427
00:24:03,242 --> 00:24:04,301
'Cause I fired him.

428
00:24:05,210 --> 00:24:07,202
It was time to move on,
you know what I'm saying?

429
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:08,338
(SCOFFS)

430
00:24:08,447 --> 00:24:09,506
You sure about that?

431
00:24:09,949 --> 00:24:12,111
- I'm not buying it.
- Not buying what?

432
00:24:12,318 --> 00:24:13,411
This.

433
00:24:14,253 --> 00:24:15,253
You.

434
00:24:15,621 --> 00:24:17,817
Firing Alfred. What
are you trying to prove?

435
00:24:19,591 --> 00:24:21,970
MAN 1: I saw her first. MAN 2:
The lady was speaking with me.

436
00:24:21,994 --> 00:24:23,428
(MEN GRUNTING)

437
00:24:23,796 --> 00:24:24,957
Hey, hey.

438
00:24:26,365 --> 00:24:27,663
(MAN GROANS)

439
00:24:27,766 --> 00:24:28,859
(GLASS SHATTERS)

440
00:24:29,768 --> 00:24:30,768
Silly boys.

441
00:24:31,370 --> 00:24:32,930
I'm really not sure
what got into them.

442
00:24:34,006 --> 00:24:35,133
You should leave.

443
00:24:36,642 --> 00:24:37,974
Well, that's awfully rude.

444
00:24:41,347 --> 00:24:42,576
But you always were.

445
00:24:50,322 --> 00:24:51,517
Who is that woman?

446
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:53,352
She seems to know you.

447
00:24:53,926 --> 00:24:55,121
Who cares?

448
00:24:55,928 --> 00:24:58,796
Redheads, they're
all crazy, am I right?

449
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,024
Ivy.

450
00:25:10,175 --> 00:25:11,735
I like what you've
done with the place.

451
00:25:12,044 --> 00:25:14,070
Thank you. Though, it
was hardly a challenge

452
00:25:14,179 --> 00:25:16,546
after what that crazy
bird passed for as taste.

453
00:25:17,883 --> 00:25:19,181
What brings you here, my love?

454
00:25:20,085 --> 00:25:21,085
Actually, you know,

455
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:23,382
I'm so proud to say that

456
00:25:23,856 --> 00:25:27,315
I seem to maintain a very good
relationship with all my exes.

457
00:25:27,393 --> 00:25:29,259
- You...
- Leave me off that list.

458
00:25:29,495 --> 00:25:31,896
Hmm. What can I
do you for, Jimmy?

459
00:25:32,498 --> 00:25:33,864
The Doc? You know him?

460
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:35,561
Oh.

461
00:25:37,269 --> 00:25:38,362
The Doc.

462
00:25:38,537 --> 00:25:41,200
I believe he was the target
of an assassination attempt

463
00:25:41,306 --> 00:25:42,831
in The Narrows this morning.

464
00:25:42,975 --> 00:25:46,036
Do you now? And you
want to protect the Doc?

465
00:25:46,712 --> 00:25:48,510
I wanna know who
wanted to kill him and why.

466
00:25:48,580 --> 00:25:49,741
You know him or not?

467
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:51,748
Oh, I know the Doc.

468
00:25:52,518 --> 00:25:53,577
Dangerous character.

469
00:25:53,819 --> 00:25:54,819
Someone like that,

470
00:25:54,887 --> 00:25:57,550
you might wanna shoot
first then ask questions later.

471
00:25:57,723 --> 00:25:58,918
Something you're good at.

472
00:26:00,392 --> 00:26:02,088
- Where is he?
- With Ed Nygma.

473
00:26:02,227 --> 00:26:03,422
They're partners.

474
00:26:04,363 --> 00:26:05,831
- Where?
- The Narrows.

475
00:26:05,898 --> 00:26:07,560
Place called Cherry's.

476
00:26:07,933 --> 00:26:09,231
Careful, Jim.

477
00:26:10,769 --> 00:26:14,206
Sometimes we search for
things we don't wish to find.

478
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:23,781
- (CELL PHONE RINGING)
- Harper, what's up?

479
00:26:23,882 --> 00:26:25,527
HARPER: <i>I'm at a murder
scene in The Narrows.</i>

480
00:26:25,551 --> 00:26:26,671
I'm busy, can you handle it?

481
00:26:26,752 --> 00:26:28,396
<i>You're gonna wanna
check this out in person.</i>

482
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:29,911
<i>I have the suspect in custody.</i>

483
00:26:30,422 --> 00:26:31,617
<i>Alfred Pennyworth.</i>

484
00:26:32,491 --> 00:26:33,491
(HANGS UP)

485
00:26:33,592 --> 00:26:34,890
(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)

486
00:26:38,263 --> 00:26:39,287
HARPER: <i>Beaten to death.</i>

487
00:26:39,765 --> 00:26:40,892
Local girl.

488
00:26:41,166 --> 00:26:43,260
Garbage collectors found
her about an hour ago,

489
00:26:43,502 --> 00:26:45,662
she lived with her boyfriend
who was at work all night.

490
00:26:45,771 --> 00:26:47,082
He told us that him
and Pennyworth

491
00:26:47,106 --> 00:26:48,106
got into it earlier.

492
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:49,617
Says that he was
trying to keep him

493
00:26:49,641 --> 00:26:50,939
separate from his girlfriend,

494
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:53,272
says that he made
advances towards the victim.

495
00:26:53,645 --> 00:26:55,807
According to him,
Pennyworth got rough.

496
00:26:55,914 --> 00:26:57,746
Rough? That doesn't
sound like him.

497
00:26:57,816 --> 00:26:59,580
Come on, you and
I both have seen

498
00:26:59,651 --> 00:27:00,812
Alfred lose his temper.

499
00:27:02,321 --> 00:27:03,414
There's more.

500
00:27:04,156 --> 00:27:05,715
This was found next to the body.

501
00:27:05,791 --> 00:27:07,282
It's an SAS signet ring.

502
00:27:07,826 --> 00:27:09,556
Impressions of it are
on the victim's face.

503
00:27:23,709 --> 00:27:24,802
My God.

504
00:27:26,945 --> 00:27:28,004
Thanks.

505
00:27:31,016 --> 00:27:32,040
Give us a minute.

506
00:27:36,121 --> 00:27:37,145
Is this yours?

507
00:27:39,324 --> 00:27:41,225
- Yes, but I...
- You hit this girl?

508
00:27:41,360 --> 00:27:42,360
No.

509
00:27:42,828 --> 00:27:45,024
How could you even ask
that? It was the boyfriend.

510
00:27:45,397 --> 00:27:46,474
I mean, he's beat her before,

511
00:27:46,498 --> 00:27:47,938
now he's gone and
bloody killed her.

512
00:27:48,300 --> 00:27:49,344
He says you were
fighting with him.

513
00:27:49,368 --> 00:27:50,461
Because he beat her!

514
00:27:50,836 --> 00:27:52,429
I swear, he's a liar.

515
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:53,528
All right, calm down.

516
00:27:53,639 --> 00:27:54,949
You're in enough
trouble as it is.

517
00:27:54,973 --> 00:27:57,340
The last thing you need
to do is lose your temper.

518
00:27:57,843 --> 00:27:59,175
Who was this girl to you?

519
00:28:00,479 --> 00:28:01,640
She was a friend.

520
00:28:04,283 --> 00:28:05,342
Just a friend.

521
00:28:06,718 --> 00:28:07,777
What, you just met her?

522
00:28:07,853 --> 00:28:09,330
Well, I know you find this
hard to believe, Gordon,

523
00:28:09,354 --> 00:28:10,515
but we connected.

524
00:28:11,890 --> 00:28:14,018
She was a beautiful, kind soul.

525
00:28:16,195 --> 00:28:18,426
Her murderer's
name is Rooney, right,

526
00:28:18,530 --> 00:28:20,396
- Gil Rooney.
- He has an alibi.

527
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:23,995
I swear to God, I'm gonna
kill that son of a bitch!

528
00:28:24,069 --> 00:28:25,662
Calm down.

529
00:28:26,104 --> 00:28:27,367
Take a breath.

530
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:29,874
Go with Harper to the precinct,

531
00:28:30,542 --> 00:28:31,566
make a statement.

532
00:28:32,578 --> 00:28:33,618
I'll find you later, yeah?

533
00:28:33,712 --> 00:28:35,578
And you're gonna arrest
Rooney as well, yeah?

534
00:28:35,681 --> 00:28:38,207
- He will make a statement, yes.
- HARPER: Cap.

535
00:28:43,922 --> 00:28:44,946
Got a witness who saw

536
00:28:45,057 --> 00:28:46,817
Pennyworth and the
boyfriend getting into it.

537
00:28:46,892 --> 00:28:48,918
- She saw the whole thing.
- GORDON: All right.

538
00:28:49,228 --> 00:28:50,992
Take Alfred back
to the precinct.

539
00:28:51,063 --> 00:28:52,554
I'll come by after my last stop.

540
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:54,859
Okay, where is he?

541
00:29:01,106 --> 00:29:02,404
Damn it.

542
00:29:10,549 --> 00:29:11,549
(MAN CLEARS THROAT)

543
00:29:16,188 --> 00:29:17,417
Tabitha.

544
00:29:18,290 --> 00:29:19,417
Butch?

545
00:29:22,294 --> 00:29:23,489
Oh, my God, it worked.

546
00:29:24,396 --> 00:29:26,422
It hurt, I'll tell you that.

547
00:29:26,999 --> 00:29:28,262
What happened to you?

548
00:29:29,268 --> 00:29:31,260
And who turned
you into this thing?

549
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:32,965
BUTCH: I don't remember much.

550
00:29:33,772 --> 00:29:35,604
I remember Barbara
shooting me in the head.

551
00:29:36,408 --> 00:29:38,138
Something in that
swamp brought me back.

552
00:29:39,978 --> 00:29:41,105
I'm a monster.

553
00:29:43,348 --> 00:29:44,509
(SIGHS)

554
00:29:51,923 --> 00:29:53,221
I came here...

555
00:29:55,961 --> 00:29:57,293
Butch, tell me.

556
00:29:59,798 --> 00:30:00,925
I came here

557
00:30:01,300 --> 00:30:03,428
because the one thing
that's still very clear

558
00:30:03,502 --> 00:30:06,131
in this thick head of mine

559
00:30:06,638 --> 00:30:07,970
is my feelings for you.

560
00:30:12,110 --> 00:30:13,476
I still love you, Tabby.

561
00:30:17,082 --> 00:30:18,277
(SIGHS)

562
00:30:23,388 --> 00:30:24,515
Okay.

563
00:30:25,657 --> 00:30:26,681
Goodbye, Tabby.

564
00:30:31,129 --> 00:30:32,969
- Thank you for waiting.
- (INDISTINCT CHATTER)

565
00:30:33,565 --> 00:30:35,363
It's worth it, you'll see.

566
00:30:36,034 --> 00:30:37,468
Believe in her passion,

567
00:30:38,203 --> 00:30:40,069
and your champion, she'll be.

568
00:30:40,672 --> 00:30:44,200
Bombs can't stop
her, nor bullets, too.

569
00:30:44,409 --> 00:30:47,004
'Cause she's here to
speak out and fight for you.

570
00:30:47,079 --> 00:30:48,240
(CROWD CHEERING)

571
00:30:48,347 --> 00:30:49,679
Ready to battle,

572
00:30:50,015 --> 00:30:51,142
ready to rock.

573
00:30:52,184 --> 00:30:53,675
People of The Narrows,

574
00:30:53,985 --> 00:30:55,146
here's the Doc.

575
00:30:55,721 --> 00:30:57,781
(CROWD CHEERING)

576
00:30:57,856 --> 00:31:00,121
CROWD: (CHANTING) Doc, Doc, Doc.

577
00:31:00,192 --> 00:31:02,127
Doc, Doc, Doc.

578
00:31:02,194 --> 00:31:03,685
Doc, Doc, Doc.

579
00:31:13,805 --> 00:31:16,468
CROWD: (CHANTING) Doc, Doc, Doc.

580
00:31:18,810 --> 00:31:20,642
This morning,
someone tried to kill me.

581
00:31:20,812 --> 00:31:21,973
(CROWD EXCLAIMING)

582
00:31:22,180 --> 00:31:23,978
Maybe it was someone
from the outside,

583
00:31:24,783 --> 00:31:26,217
maybe it was one of you.

584
00:31:26,284 --> 00:31:27,284
CROWD: No, no way.

585
00:31:27,619 --> 00:31:29,850
LEE: You know what? I
don't know. And I don't care.

586
00:31:30,288 --> 00:31:31,620
But what I do know

587
00:31:32,457 --> 00:31:36,690
is that someone did not
like what I was saying.

588
00:31:37,396 --> 00:31:40,560
Now why would the
idea of a united Narrows

589
00:31:41,032 --> 00:31:42,125
scare people?

590
00:31:43,135 --> 00:31:44,728
I'll tell you why.

591
00:31:45,203 --> 00:31:49,538
Because a united Narrows
is a strong Narrows.

592
00:31:49,641 --> 00:31:50,904
(CROWD CHEERING)

593
00:31:50,976 --> 00:31:52,035
Guess what?

594
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:55,570
They should be scared.

595
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:58,047
(CROWD CHEERING)

596
00:31:58,116 --> 00:31:59,550
Magnificent, isn't she?

597
00:32:00,419 --> 00:32:03,184
- It's been forever, right?
- I should bust you, right now.

598
00:32:03,255 --> 00:32:06,589
Oh, come on, Jim, don't be
grumpy. Your ex has my full support.

599
00:32:06,691 --> 00:32:08,557
She's really gonna
change things around here.

600
00:32:08,627 --> 00:32:11,028
Someone hired Griffin
Krank to kill her this morning.

601
00:32:11,096 --> 00:32:12,573
You really think they
won't do it again?

602
00:32:12,597 --> 00:32:13,597
Krank?

603
00:32:13,698 --> 00:32:15,394
A toy maker but
also an assassin.

604
00:32:15,634 --> 00:32:16,634
(CHUCKLES)

605
00:32:17,068 --> 00:32:18,764
That is so Gotham.

606
00:32:18,870 --> 00:32:23,433
Because together we have
the power to change our lives.

607
00:32:23,575 --> 00:32:26,044
CROWD: Yeah! MAN: That's right.

608
00:32:26,211 --> 00:32:30,342
LEE: Imagine a
hospital, imagine schools.

609
00:32:31,516 --> 00:32:34,953
Imagine these slums torn down.

610
00:32:35,086 --> 00:32:36,645
(CROWD CHEERING)

611
00:32:36,755 --> 00:32:38,951
Your children deserve better.

612
00:32:39,024 --> 00:32:41,755
Your children deserve life!

613
00:32:41,827 --> 00:32:44,126
(CHEERING)

614
00:32:45,597 --> 00:32:46,597
Yeah!

615
00:32:47,299 --> 00:32:48,597
(CROWD CHEERING)

616
00:33:03,415 --> 00:33:04,415
Jim.

617
00:33:04,983 --> 00:33:06,076
Doc.

618
00:33:06,151 --> 00:33:07,728
I like to think of that
as a sign of respect,

619
00:33:07,752 --> 00:33:09,414
not just a lack of imagination.

620
00:33:10,956 --> 00:33:12,151
How long you been back?

621
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:15,085
A while.

622
00:33:17,596 --> 00:33:19,155
I wish you would
have contacted me.

623
00:33:20,499 --> 00:33:21,523
I've been busy.

624
00:33:23,168 --> 00:33:24,261
I can see that.

625
00:33:27,105 --> 00:33:28,266
You look great.

626
00:33:31,243 --> 00:33:32,506
You look the same.

627
00:33:35,413 --> 00:33:37,075
Are you here to arrest someone?

628
00:33:37,415 --> 00:33:38,474
- Me?
- (NYGMA CHUCKLES)

629
00:33:40,085 --> 00:33:41,917
I'm here because
someone wants you dead.

630
00:33:43,088 --> 00:33:45,250
The assassin's
still on the loose,

631
00:33:45,757 --> 00:33:48,591
as is the person who
hired him. You're not safe.

632
00:33:50,061 --> 00:33:52,690
It's Gotham, is
anyone ever safe?

633
00:33:56,434 --> 00:33:58,096
So, you're partners
with Ed, huh?

634
00:33:59,337 --> 00:34:00,361
Why?

635
00:34:00,839 --> 00:34:01,839
I'm right here.

636
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:03,133
Why not?

637
00:34:04,209 --> 00:34:05,871
Wouldn't have
been my first choice,

638
00:34:05,977 --> 00:34:07,969
but the universe has funny ways.

639
00:34:08,380 --> 00:34:09,507
Still here.

640
00:34:12,684 --> 00:34:14,016
I'll see you around, Jim.

641
00:34:19,391 --> 00:34:21,826
I'm gonna take a look around.

642
00:34:29,200 --> 00:34:30,200
That's...

643
00:34:35,807 --> 00:34:36,807
Oh, boy.

644
00:34:50,555 --> 00:34:52,990
I've been trying to get to you.

645
00:34:53,558 --> 00:34:55,550
(PANTING)

646
00:35:03,368 --> 00:35:05,098
You shouldn't be here,
you're a wanted man.

647
00:35:07,439 --> 00:35:09,119
Better stay cool on
me. I've got friends...

648
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:11,232
- (GROANS)
- That was for Tiffany.

649
00:35:11,710 --> 00:35:12,710
(GROANS)

650
00:35:12,777 --> 00:35:14,370
- And that was for me.
- Help me!

651
00:35:15,213 --> 00:35:18,240
This man killed my
girlfriend. He's a maniac.

652
00:35:19,150 --> 00:35:20,709
- (GLASS SHATTERS)
- (GROANS)

653
00:35:33,665 --> 00:35:35,133
You're making this too easy.

654
00:35:35,200 --> 00:35:37,760
I'll just tell the cops
this was self-defense.

655
00:35:39,270 --> 00:35:41,330
(MEN GROANING)

656
00:35:45,677 --> 00:35:48,511
Sorry, it took me so
long, I was in the john.

657
00:35:55,053 --> 00:35:57,147
I liked you better when
you were making tea.

658
00:35:57,889 --> 00:35:58,889
(PANTING)

659
00:35:58,990 --> 00:35:59,990
Harvey,

660
00:36:00,625 --> 00:36:01,936
what the bloody hell
are you doing here?

661
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:02,960
I work here.

662
00:36:03,294 --> 00:36:05,490
Don't say it like that,
this place has history.

663
00:36:05,697 --> 00:36:08,326
I love bartending, it involves
two of my favorite things,

664
00:36:08,667 --> 00:36:10,863
- drinking and ignoring people.
- (CHUCKLES)

665
00:36:11,336 --> 00:36:12,599
Who are these jokers?

666
00:36:14,039 --> 00:36:16,031
Oh, he's a bloody murderer.

667
00:36:16,341 --> 00:36:18,503
Then call a cop,
I'm a bartender.

668
00:36:18,677 --> 00:36:20,202
No, he's the murderer.

669
00:36:20,311 --> 00:36:22,212
- I have an alibi.
- HARVEY: Oh! Yeah?

670
00:36:22,514 --> 00:36:24,881
Let me guess, one of
these guys is your alibi?

671
00:36:27,852 --> 00:36:30,287
- What do you say now, pal?
- Oh, I'm not an alibi.

672
00:36:31,022 --> 00:36:32,183
I'll call it in.

673
00:36:43,835 --> 00:36:45,030
(CREAKING)

674
00:37:12,063 --> 00:37:13,087
IVY: Hi, kitty-cat.

675
00:37:16,768 --> 00:37:19,237
You suck at following
people, by the way.

676
00:37:25,276 --> 00:37:26,403
Ivy?

677
00:37:27,412 --> 00:37:28,573
In the flesh.

678
00:37:30,248 --> 00:37:31,511
Just different flesh.

679
00:37:32,050 --> 00:37:33,382
What happened to you?

680
00:37:35,186 --> 00:37:36,210
(SCOFFS)

681
00:37:38,089 --> 00:37:39,717
Something wonderful.

682
00:37:48,166 --> 00:37:49,464
(GROANS SOFTLY)

683
00:37:51,803 --> 00:37:53,271
Can you feel that?

684
00:37:54,105 --> 00:37:55,903
Coursing through your veins,

685
00:37:57,575 --> 00:37:58,599
it's my essence.

686
00:38:02,614 --> 00:38:03,946
Is your head swimming?

687
00:38:05,450 --> 00:38:08,249
Your mouth drying up?

688
00:38:09,387 --> 00:38:10,878
It lives within me now.

689
00:38:12,557 --> 00:38:13,650
This power.

690
00:38:13,758 --> 00:38:14,953
(GROANING)

691
00:38:18,429 --> 00:38:19,429
Drink.

692
00:38:20,231 --> 00:38:21,631
It'll counteract the toxin.

693
00:38:28,406 --> 00:38:29,965
It took me a few tries,

694
00:38:31,676 --> 00:38:32,939
but it'll work.

695
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:35,837
(COUGHS)

696
00:38:37,315 --> 00:38:38,315
See?

697
00:38:38,416 --> 00:38:39,748
(SELINA PANTING)

698
00:38:39,818 --> 00:38:40,979
You have to trust me.

699
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:43,544
You've gone crazy.

700
00:38:43,655 --> 00:38:45,851
No, I haven't.

701
00:38:49,327 --> 00:38:50,989
I've been reborn.

702
00:38:51,696 --> 00:38:54,131
And I will never
be underestimated

703
00:38:54,199 --> 00:38:55,827
or ignored ever again.

704
00:38:57,802 --> 00:38:59,862
You always looked
after me, Selina.

705
00:39:02,373 --> 00:39:04,535
Now, let me help you.

706
00:39:12,550 --> 00:39:14,451
Let's make Gotham our bitch.

707
00:39:18,990 --> 00:39:20,356
Please, don't hurt me.

708
00:39:20,525 --> 00:39:22,050
Why would I do that?

709
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:24,852
You tried to kill Lee.

710
00:39:25,063 --> 00:39:27,794
Yeah, because you paid me to.

711
00:39:27,866 --> 00:39:29,027
What?

712
00:39:29,133 --> 00:39:31,534
You paid me good
money to kill the Doc.

713
00:39:31,803 --> 00:39:34,363
Used your alias, the Riddler.

714
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:39,874
(LAUGHING)

715
00:39:46,851 --> 00:39:49,218
You want me to
finish the job or not?

716
00:39:51,522 --> 00:39:52,546
I came to you?

717
00:39:53,892 --> 00:39:55,019
Paid in cash.

718
00:39:55,260 --> 00:39:57,058
Said the Doc was
holding you back,

719
00:39:57,528 --> 00:40:00,293
she has to die, or
you can't be free.

720
00:40:00,431 --> 00:40:01,455
Oh, God.

721
00:40:01,566 --> 00:40:04,559
I put myself at
great risk for you.

722
00:40:04,736 --> 00:40:07,706
Cops came to my workshop,
I can't go back there.

723
00:40:07,772 --> 00:40:09,536
- My son...
- Let go of him!

724
00:40:09,607 --> 00:40:10,700
Get down, Ed!

725
00:40:12,610 --> 00:40:14,688
What the hell were you
thinking, going after him alone?

726
00:40:14,712 --> 00:40:16,408
Well, clearly I wasn't thinking.

727
00:40:16,581 --> 00:40:17,776
(NYGMA EXHALES)

728
00:40:20,118 --> 00:40:21,245
Damn it.

729
00:40:23,521 --> 00:40:25,121
Did he say anything
about who hired him?

730
00:40:26,958 --> 00:40:28,517
(STAMMERS) It was him, all him.

731
00:40:28,593 --> 00:40:30,193
He was a lone wolf.
That's what he said.

732
00:40:30,261 --> 00:40:33,459
He was afraid of what Lee
was gonna do to The Narrows.

733
00:40:33,564 --> 00:40:35,409
Are you sure? His son said
he was talking to somebody

734
00:40:35,433 --> 00:40:36,731
on the phone about the Doc.

735
00:40:37,268 --> 00:40:38,913
(STAMMERS) He said
that he was calling around

736
00:40:38,937 --> 00:40:40,414
trying to get support, but
no one would help him.

737
00:40:40,438 --> 00:40:41,770
So he went alone. Crazy.

738
00:40:42,106 --> 00:40:43,267
Crazy loon.

739
00:40:43,574 --> 00:40:44,598
He told you all that?

740
00:40:45,276 --> 00:40:46,676
Honestly, I'm not
much of a threat.

741
00:40:47,278 --> 00:40:49,179
I'm so lucky that you
came out here, Jim,

742
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:50,391
I don't know what
I would have done.

743
00:40:50,415 --> 00:40:51,474
This is Captain Gordon.

744
00:40:52,116 --> 00:40:54,347
I have a suspect down,
outside Cherry's place,

745
00:40:54,452 --> 00:40:55,818
on State Street, in The Narrows.

746
00:40:56,854 --> 00:40:58,413
Send all available units.

747
00:41:01,793 --> 00:41:03,421
Nice job, Ed, I guess.

748
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:10,359
I'm back. (LAUGHS)

749
00:41:15,773 --> 00:41:17,674
(POLICE RADIO CHATTER)

750
00:41:20,945 --> 00:41:21,969
OFFICER: Move.

751
00:41:27,285 --> 00:41:29,125
HARVEY: Of all the
beer halls in the city, huh?

752
00:41:30,088 --> 00:41:31,681
Who was it that
that jerk killed?

753
00:41:31,923 --> 00:41:32,947
(DOOR CLOSES)

754
00:41:33,791 --> 00:41:34,815
A lady.

755
00:41:36,828 --> 00:41:38,091
Very beautiful.

756
00:41:38,997 --> 00:41:40,659
Kind, nice lady.

757
00:41:42,834 --> 00:41:44,166
Then I drink to her.

758
00:41:50,074 --> 00:41:51,201
(DOOR OPENS)

759
00:41:54,712 --> 00:41:56,237
Heard the call on the radio.

760
00:41:59,684 --> 00:42:01,084
Don't worry, we'll
get him to talk.

761
00:42:06,357 --> 00:42:07,586
How you been?

762
00:42:08,826 --> 00:42:10,021
Awesome.

763
00:42:18,369 --> 00:42:19,632
I've missed you.

764
00:42:24,042 --> 00:42:25,374
Is that so?

765
00:42:28,146 --> 00:42:29,478
Well, I haven't missed you.

766
00:42:30,715 --> 00:42:32,359
I haven't missed begging
you not to do something

767
00:42:32,383 --> 00:42:34,103
just to watch you go
ahead and do it anyway.

768
00:42:34,752 --> 00:42:37,483
Haven't missed watching
you bang Falcone's daughter,

769
00:42:37,555 --> 00:42:39,387
while she uses you
to get rid of Penguin.

770
00:42:41,359 --> 00:42:42,725
Something's eating at you, Jim.

771
00:42:43,094 --> 00:42:44,153
I don't know what it is,

772
00:42:44,228 --> 00:42:45,748
but you're no good
at keeping secrets.

773
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:48,859
And you're not gonna feel
clean till you get it off your chest.

774
00:42:50,902 --> 00:42:53,371
You didn't come down here
because you miss me as a cop.

775
00:42:54,272 --> 00:42:55,934
You came here to confess.

776
00:42:56,407 --> 00:42:58,774
You want me to be your
priest. Well, sorry, pal.

777
00:42:59,744 --> 00:43:01,212
I'm not interested.

778
00:43:04,215 --> 00:43:05,410
So hit the bricks,

779
00:43:06,150 --> 00:43:07,413
take that with you.

780
00:44:00,438 --> 00:44:01,438
English - SDH
